{"verdict":"needs-changes","summary":"The diff narrows the clear range in repaint_history_tail from [0, viewport.y) to [top, visible_rows), leaving stale duplicate copies of screen-resident history lines at rows [0, top) that the pre-diff code correctly erased.","findings":[{"file":"crates/mu-solo/src/viewport.rs","line":651,"severity":"high","issue":"Narrowing the clear loop from `0..viewport.y` to `top..visible_rows` leaves rows [0, top) uncleared. In the shrink-after-stream scenario (viewport grows during streaming, insert_before commits the turn at the grown y, then set_height shrinks back at turn commit — the common inline-mode path), scrollback_committed is stale (= history.len() - old_y from the last insert_before at the grown viewport), so start = scrollback_committed, rows_to_draw = old_y, and top = new_y - old_y > 0. The rows [0, top) still hold the OLD screen-resident tail written by that insert_before (history[scrollback_committed..scrollback_committed+top]), and the repaint loop redraws the SAME tail at [top, new_y). Each of the first `top` history lines thus appears twice on screen — once at its old position and once in the repainted span. The pre-diff full clear of [0, viewport.y) produced a blank band at [0, top), but that blank band is CORRECT: there are only `old_y` screen-resident lines for `new_y > old_y` rows, so the top `top` rows genuinely have nothing to draw (the content is in native scrollback). The diff's rationale that [0, top) holds 'content the terminal scrolled up there' is wrong for this code path — repaint_history_tail is called after a pure logical viewport relocation (no terminal scroll), so those rows hold duplicate copies, not independently-scrolled content. The fix trades a correct blank band for a visible duplication band."}]}
